Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hi Joe!

Run the coef function in mirt to print your item parameters estimated from the model. You will have one b parameter for binary items. This is the item difficulty for that item. For your polytomous item you will have 7 item threshold parameter estimates (for an item with 8 response categories). For a traditional item difficulty estimate for that item, you can take the mean of those item threshold parameters (at least this is commonly done in health outcome measurement for polytomous items). Hope that helps.

Keri

