Thanks Keri,

Having done a bit more looking on the collapsing of categories, research suggests that as "there were no simulation conditions for which collapsing of categories significantly improved the estimation of the latent trait, the collapsing of categories is not advisable under any preventable circumstance" (http://digitool.library.mcgill.ca/webclient/StreamGate?folder_id=0&dvs=1553098171390~937, p. 79). This is even in a case (like mine) where categories appear entirely 'submerged' in an ICCC graphic.

I am therefore attempting to avoid collapsing categories!

But, this means I am still in the position where: all response categories available are informing "F1" values in a logical manner (as shown in a table in a previous image); but, difficulty estimates "b" are not logical/do not correspond with my category's effects on the F1 value (as also shown in a previous image).

Are there any other possible means of obtaining item/category 'difficulty' within mirt that I could try? Or, am I just misunderstanding things more generally (which is very possible)!?

Thank you again,

Joe

